## 2. Frontend Dashboard — Complete Architecture

### 2.1 Framework & Routing

**Stack**: Next.js 14 (App Router) + React 18 + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS

The App Router uses file-system conventions for routing:

```
frontend/app/
├── layout.tsx          ← Root layout (html, body, font imports)
├── page.tsx            ← Landing page (/)
├── globals.css         ← Global styles
└── dashboard/
    ├── layout.tsx      ← Dashboard layout (sidebar + header wrapper)
    ├── page.tsx        ← SOC Overview (/dashboard)
    ├── alerts/page.tsx        ← Alert Management
    ├── topology/page.tsx      ← Full Network Map
    ├── predict/page.tsx       ← Predictive Risk
    ├── policies/page.tsx      ← NLP Policy Engine
    └── replay/page.tsx        ← Attack Replay
```

**Layout nesting**: `dashboard/layout.tsx` wraps all `/dashboard/*` pages with the persistent sidebar and header. Navigation between dashboard pages only re-renders the content area — the sidebar/header stay mounted.

### 2.2 Frontend Dependencies

| Package | Version | Purpose |
|---------|---------|---------|
| `next` | 14.2.35 | React meta-framework |
| `react` | ^18 | UI library |
| `d3` | ^7.9.0 | Low-level SVG data visualization (network topology) |
| `recharts` | ^3.7.0 | Declarative React chart components (trust timeline) |
| `@visx/heatmap` + `@visx/scale` | ^3.12.0 | SVG heatmap primitives (drift calendar) |
| `framer-motion` | ^12.34.3 | Animation library (page transitions, micro-interactions) |
| `socket.io-client` | ^4.8.3 | Real-time WebSocket connection to backend |
| `lucide-react` | ^0.575.0 | Icon library (Shield, AlertTriangle, Activity, etc.) |
| `zustand` | ^5.0.11 | State management (installed but not yet used) |
| `clsx` + `tailwind-merge` | Latest | Conditional CSS class composition |

### 2.3 The Three Core Visualizations

#### A. Network Topology Map — D3.js Force-Directed Graph

**File**: [NetworkTopologyMap.tsx](file:///d:/coding_files/Projects/DeviceDNA/frontend/components/visualizations/NetworkTopologyMap.tsx) (9,033 bytes)

This is the centerpiece visualization. It renders all 50 devices as nodes in an interactive force-directed graph:

- **Force simulation**: `d3.forceSimulation()` with charge repulsion, link attraction, center gravity, and collision prevention
- **Node coloring**: Green (score ≥ 80), Yellow (40-79), Red (< 40) with animated glow on anomalous nodes
- **Node sizing**: Scales with traffic volume
- **Interactions**: Drag nodes to reposition, click to drill into device details
- **Live updates**: WebSocket `telemetry_ping` events animate edge pulses between communicating nodes

**Current state**: Generates its own 50 mock nodes with randomized positions and trust scores. Does NOT fetch from the backend API.

#### B. Trust Score Timeline — Recharts Line Chart

**File**: [TrustScoreTimeline.tsx](file:///d:/coding_files/Projects/DeviceDNA/frontend/components/visualizations/TrustScoreTimeline.tsx) (6,936 bytes)

- **Data**: 12-hour history with trust score data points every 5 minutes
- **Threshold lines**: Horizontal reference lines at score 40 (suspicious) and 80 (trusted)
- **Live updates**: When `new_alert` WebSocket events arrive, the chart drops the affected device's score and shows a recovery curve
- **Area fill**: Green gradient fill under the score line, switching to red when below threshold

**Current state**: Self-generates mock timeseries data. WebSocket events trigger visual score drops.

#### C. CUSUM Drift Heatmap — visx Calendar Grid

**File**: [DriftHeatmap.tsx](file:///d:/coding_files/Projects/DeviceDNA/frontend/components/visualizations/DriftHeatmap.tsx) (5,082 bytes)

- **Layout**: 7 columns (days) × 24 rows (hours) = 168 cells
- **Color scale**: White (no drift) → Yellow (mild) → Orange (moderate) → Red (severe)
- **Mock pattern**: Simulates attack signatures on Tuesday/Wednesday nights (elevated drift scores from 11 PM – 3 AM)
- **Tooltips**: Custom hover tooltips showing exact drift score, day, and hour

### 2.4 Layout Components

- [Sidebar.tsx](file:///d:/coding_files/Projects/DeviceDNA/frontend/components/layout/Sidebar.tsx) — Navigation sidebar with icons for each dashboard page (Overview, Topology, Alerts, Predict, Policies, Replay)
- [Header.tsx](file:///d:/coding_files/Projects/DeviceDNA/frontend/components/layout/Header.tsx) — Top bar with search, notifications bell, and user avatar

### 2.5 Landing Page

The root [page.tsx](file:///d:/coding_files/Projects/DeviceDNA/frontend/app/page.tsx) (15,947 bytes) is a premium glassmorphism landing page with:
- Animated gradient background
- API status indicator (fetches `/api/health` from backend)
- Hero section with platform description
- Feature cards with hover effects
- Framer Motion entrance animations

### 2.6 WebSocket Integration

The frontend connects to `http://localhost:8000` using `socket.io-client`. Events handled:

```typescript
socket.on('new_alert', (data) => {
  // Add to alert queue, flash node on topology map
  // Drop trust score on timeline chart
});

socket.on('telemetry_ping', (data) => {
  // Animate edge pulse on D3 network map
});

socket.on('device_isolated', (data) => {
  // Show success notification, gray out node
});
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> All dashboard pages currently use **local `useState` hooks** for state management. The installed Zustand store (`frontend/store/`) is empty. There is no centralized API client (`lib/api.ts`) — only the landing page health check makes a real backend API call.

